From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: holtwood-systems <dev@holtwood-systems.invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hicache): export storage prefetch outcome stats
 dynamically

Revive #36280 on current main, following the coordination ask in the
#36474 review ("please coordinate with #36280" for the event-count
export of `_prefetch_outcome_stats`).

UnifiedRadixCache maintains 14 cumulative prefetch-outcome counters and
snapshots them onto StorageMetrics in check_hicache_events, but the
collector never exports them: declined/revoked prefetches are only
visible through the #37503 token-dimension series, with no event counts.

Instead of enumerating outcomes (the original branch hardcoded 6 keys
and went stale when the dict grew to 14), export the snapshot
dynamically:

- every snapshot key becomes an `outcome` label, routed by unit: keys
  ending in `_tokens` go to `storage_prefetch_outcome_tokens_total`,
  everything else to `storage_prefetch_outcome_events_total`, named to
  sit with the #37503 `storage_prefetch_*` family;
- the source counters are cumulative on the cache side and may be reset
  with the cache, so exports are monotonic deltas: a lower snapshot
  starts a new epoch that re-exports its current value, never a
  negative delta (carried over from #36280);
- `prefetch_stats` is now a declared StorageMetrics field rather than a
  dynamically injected attribute; the check_hicache_events feed assigns
  it unconditionally, and a None/absent field is a no-op instead of an
  AttributeError once the field is formalized.

Tests cover monotonic-delta/new-epoch export, key dynamism (outcomes
beyond the original six export unchanged), unit routing, and the
None/absent-snapshot no-op.

Credit: the delta/new-epoch export discipline and the original test
scenario come from #36280 by @yikun-c.

Closes #35808 (revives the slice originally landed as #36280)
